WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.040
Speaker 1: this is super interesting.

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:07.490
We've been talking about declining interest
in vaccination.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:12.849
The people who already have been vaccinated
are mostly people who really wanted to be

00:00:12.849 --> 00:00:13.849
vaccinated.

00:00:13.849 --> 00:00:19.141
And now we have a situation where supply is
starting to exceed demand and a government

00:00:19.141 --> 00:00:24.550
state governments need to figure out new ways
to get people interested in getting vaccinated

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:29.019
because remember, no matter what anybody tells
you, there's no mandatory vaccination per

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:30.019
governments.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:32.770
There are certain schools that will say if
you want to come to campus, you have to go

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:37.510
and get a vaccine or if you want to work for
us, you have to go and get a vaccine.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:43.430
But there are no mandatory vaccinations per
the federal, state or municipal governments.

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:47.280
But you have an interest from governments,
state governments.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.380
They want to be open and they want to be open
in a way where people aren't going to get

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.030
sick because that's what's best for business.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.670
So they're thinking of new ways to encourage
people to get vaccinated.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:04.150
Republican Ohio Gov. Mike DeWine is creating
five one million dollar basically lottery

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:07.140
rewards for people who get vaccinated.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:12.310
Five people who get vaccinated in Ohio are
going to win a million dollars each.

00:01:12.310 --> 00:01:17.740
The Republican governor announced this last
night all vaccinated adults will be eligible

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:24.370
to enter a lottery that will pay out one million
dollars each to five winners starting just

00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:28.220
a couple of weeks from today, March 20th,
May 26th, rather.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:35.450
And separately, DeWine is also offering five
vaccinated teenagers full ride scholarships

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:40.380
to the state's public universities, including
tuition, room, board and textbooks.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.640
The textbooks are key.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.630
Oftentimes you hear free tuition, right?

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.240
But what about the thousands of dollars for
textbooks?

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:52.180
It will even include that, DeWine said in
a statewide address, quote, I know some may

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:53.840
say, DeWine, you're crazy.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:58.760
The million dollar drawing idea of yours is
a waste of money, but truly the real waste

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:04.080
at this point in the pandemic when the vaccine
is readily available to anyone who wants it,

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.790
is a life lost to covid-19.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.279
I think that this is absolutely fantastic.

00:02:10.279 --> 00:02:18.739
And understand that you have money set aside
already in a number of different states for

00:02:18.739 --> 00:02:23.389
vaccination and for getting people vaccinated
and public awareness campaigns.

00:02:23.389 --> 00:02:30.319
This is a way of using five million of that
dollars instead of on billboards and TV ads

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:31.319
or whatever the case may be.

00:02:31.319 --> 00:02:34.120
You're just saying, well, let's just give
five million plus the cost of tuition to the

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.989
five teenagers, to some people.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.739
And I think it's absolutely fantastic.

00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:43.739
The lottery payout will be funded using federal
coronavirus relief money allocated to the

00:02:43.739 --> 00:02:44.980
states.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.230
States and localities have been given this
money by the Treasury.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.290
They've been given wide discretion about how
to spend it.

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:53.769
And Mike DeWine is saying, let's give it to
some people.

00:02:53.769 --> 00:02:57.040
There are questions as to how effective public
health officials think that this is going

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.040
to be.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:03.860
Tara Smith, who teaches epidemiology at Kent
State University, says there's some research

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:09.099
to suggest small financial incentives could
increase vaccine rates, but that just giving

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:16.290
a million dollars to five people may not work
because of the perceived odds of winning are

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.480
relatively low.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:23.750
And that if there is a criticism of it, that
was my thought, which is a million dollars

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:27.090
for five people, that's a lot.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:31.019
But what about giving one hundred thousand
dollars to 50 people?

00:03:31.019 --> 00:03:34.760
It's the same amount of money, but I think
the perceived odds of winning will be higher.

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.909
And of course, they will be they would be
10 times higher.

00:03:37.909 --> 00:03:41.349
Let's listen to Mike DeWine announcing this
and talking about this yesterday

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:44.209
Speaker 2: on May 26.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:49.230
We'll announce the winner of a separate drawing
for adults, adults who have received at least

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:52.469
their first dose of the vaccine.

00:03:52.469 --> 00:03:59.150
This announcement will occur each Wednesday
for five weeks, and the winner each Wednesday

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.969
will receive one million dollars.

00:04:01.969 --> 00:04:04.999
Speaker 1: So I think it's a great idea.

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:11.709
Again, the only change I might make is instead
of five people get a million dollars each,

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:15.589
I might make it 50 people get a hundred thousand
dollars.

00:04:15.589 --> 00:04:16.910
And the.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:22.160
The alternative that was also proposed is
just pay everyone who gets the vaccine, figure

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.810
out how many people, how many adults you have,
divide up the five million dollar prize pool.

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:31.470
What does it work out to give that to everybody?

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:35.940
And then for the unspoken for money at the
end of the campaign, maybe then that becomes

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.590
sort of like a lottery or something like that.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.909
A lot of different ways to do this.

00:04:38.909 --> 00:04:43.250
I think it's a I have no moral problems with
it at all.

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:47.400
And if it's effective, I'm 100 percent for
it, let me know your thoughts, let me know

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:52.870
if you would go about it a slightly different
way, and we'll have more coverage of what

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:59.270
different states are doing to encourage vaccination
on our Instagram page, which you can find

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.919
at David Pakman show.

00:05:00.919 --> 00:05:03.419
You can also find me on Instagram at David
Pakman

